15. Responsive behaviour
The screenshot is a desktop-first design.

However, the implementation must also work on tablets and mobile devices.

Desktop — 1200px and above
- Header stays horizontal.
- Calendar and activities remain side by side.
- Calendar takes approximately 70% of the workspace.
- Activity panel takes approximately 30%.
Tablet — 768px to 1199px
- Reduce the calendar's minimum cell dimensions.
- Keep the activities panel visible if sufficient width exists.
- Otherwise move it below the calendar.
- Reduce title and toolbar spacing.
Mobile — below 768px
- Header becomes compact.
- Farm selector and weather widget can move to a secondary row.
- Toolbar wraps into multiple rows.
- Calendar should not cause whole-page horizontal overflow.
- Default to an agenda view with the month grid still accessible.
- Today's Activities becomes a full-width card underneath.
Suggested CSS:
.calendar-workspace {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns:
        minmax(0, 2.38fr)
        minmax(320px, 1fr);
    gap: 22px;
}

@media (max-width: 1100px) {
    .calendar-workspace {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
}

@media (max-width: 767px) {
    .calendar-grid {
        grid-template-rows: repeat(5, minmax(65px, auto));
    }

    .event-chip {
        font-size: 10px;
        padding: 4px;
    }

    .calendar-toolbar {
        height: auto;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 10px;
        padding: 12px;
    }
}



16. Important visual details that must not be overlooked
These small details are what make the screenshot feel polished rather than like a generic calendar template.
1. The background photograph remains visible around the cards.
2. The cards have a dark, slightly green-tinted glass appearance.
3. Borders are subtle and cool-toned, not bright white.
4. The calendar fills most of the available horizontal space.
5. All seven date columns have precisely equal widths.
6. The calendar has no excessive empty margins.
7. Event chips are compact, with readable two-line labels.
8. Crop and activity categories use consistent colours everywhere.
9. The selected date has a luminous green outline.
10. The Today label is a small bright-green pill.
11. The right-hand activity panel has photographic and icon thumbnails.
12. The activity rows are separated by subtle dividers.
13. Status pills use their category's accent colour.
14. The Next 7 Days section is compact, not another large card.
15. Add Task is the most prominent interactive button.
16. The month/year selector is easy to find and operate.
17. No bottom task table or unnecessary category-filter strip should be added.
18. Do not add the excluded profile icon.

17. Final implementation priority
The most important thing is to reproduce the proportions and hierarchy before spending time on decorative details.

I would implement in this order:
1. Page geometry
   
   Get the header, toolbar, 910px calendar and 383px activity panel aligned correctly.
2. Calendar grid
   
   Implement the seven-column, five-week grid, correct date placement and event rendering.
3. Today's Activities
   
   Recreate the activity thumbnails, typography, separators, badges and Next 7 Days section.
4. Glassmorphism
   
   Add the translucent backgrounds, blur, gradients, borders and shadows.
5. Interactions
   
   Connect month navigation, date selection, activity details and Add Task.
6. Responsive layout
   
   Ensure the interface remains usable on tablets and phones.
The defining design principle: the monthly calendar is the main workspace, while the right-hand panel acts as the farmer's daily operational assistant. The farmer should be able to understand the month's activity at a glance and immediately understand what needs attention today, without navigating away from the page.